WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:03.490
Abraham: The main form of unethical
conduct we think about within

00:00:03.490 --> 00:00:07.399
cyber security is hacking, but
there are other forms of unethical

00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:08.900
conduct that may take place.

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:13.799
It may involve deliberately copying
information and data to use or supply

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:15.729
to others for unethical activities.

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:19.900
Nicole: Unethical behaviour can
involve sabotage, disclosing or

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:25.000
misusing confidential information or
maliciously injuring the reputation or

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.169
prospects of an individual or business.

00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:29.729
Let’s look at this in
a little more detail.

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:34.350
Abraham: Sabotage- is rather an
obvious form of unethical conduct

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:38.479
and this can be seen when an employee
intentionally damages a system.

00:00:39.169 --> 00:00:43.879
This may be for spite or to show that they
can fix an ‘existing’ problem to showcase

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:46.630
their skills or gain a ‘bug bounty’.

00:00:47.590 --> 00:00:50.940
This may also be done by a disgruntled
employee who wants to get their

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:53.910
own back if they have an axe to
grind or have lost their job.

00:00:54.529 --> 00:00:58.139
Nicole: Disclosing of misusing
confidential information- cyber

00:00:58.139 --> 00:01:03.160
security professional have access to
a great deal of personal confidential

00:01:03.170 --> 00:01:07.280
data and may feel that it might be
worth something to pass it on to

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:09.390
someone else or use it for blackmail.

00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:13.349
Abraham: Maliciously injuring
the reputation or prospects

00:01:13.349 --> 00:01:14.949
of an individual or business.

00:01:15.699 --> 00:01:19.770
Maliciously spreading information
or images can seriously damage the

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:22.030
reputation of a colleague or business.

00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:27.080
Cyber security professionals are in a
trusted role having access to confidential

00:01:27.089 --> 00:01:31.429
data and should never use this against
someone as this is totally unethical.

00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:36.970
Nicole: But unethical conduct doesn’t
always have to be on a large scale it can

00:01:36.970 --> 00:01:41.000
also be something as simple as leaving
a 'post it' around with log in details

00:01:41.039 --> 00:01:43.329
for anyone to access a computer system.

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:48.359
Abraham: It may be thoughtless or show
a lack of judgement, but it can lead

00:01:48.390 --> 00:01:52.620
to so much more as this can open a
system up to unethical security issues.

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:57.000
Nicole: It’s also important to remember
that cyber security professionals are

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:01.360
highly trusted members of staff who have
a great deal of access to important,

00:02:01.599 --> 00:02:04.419
sensitive and highly confidential data.

00:02:04.799 --> 00:02:16.760
They should never use and abuse this
high level of access and trust placed

00:02:16.760 --> 00:02:18.644
in them by displaying unethical conduct.

